-- Aquarela & Nanquim: o teste de The Secret Garden saiu "depressivo" (rosto de adolescente de anime abatido, paleta
-- amarelo-bege, paredes oliva e madeira escura). A amostra é alegre: crianças de livro infantil e cores vivas.
update public.comic_styles set render_prompt = render_prompt || $p$

CHARACTER DESIGN — STORYBOOK, NOT ANIME (VERY IMPORTANT)
- Draw characters exactly like the style sample: classic children's-storybook design with slightly large rounded heads, round soft faces, simple bright eyes (dark pupils with one white highlight), small rounded nose, small expressive mouth and round rosy cheeks.
- Children look young, healthy and charming. Never a thin realistic teenager, never anime/manga eyes with heavy lids or long lashes, never gaunt, pale-yellow or tired-looking skin.
- Negative emotions (sulking, sour, sad, lonely) are drawn gently and cutely: pouting lips, frowning eyebrows, crossed arms, looking away. The character stays appealing and the page stays cheerful.
- If the text describes a character as pale, sallow, yellow or sickly, show it only lightly in the character (a slightly paler skin), never by tinting the whole page.

COLOR — CHEERFUL IN EVERY PANEL
- Every panel contains at least two vivid sample colors (orange, red, sky blue, leaf green, rose) and plenty of white paper.
- Interiors: light walls in cream, pale sky blue or soft pink; wallpaper with small colorful motifs; light honey wood; colorful rugs, curtains, vases and flowers. Never olive-green walls, dark wood panelling or brown corridors.
- Exteriors: bright skies, colorful flowers and foliage, light paths.
- Overall the page must feel warm, light and inviting, like the style sample, even when the story moment is sad.$p$ where id = 'aquarela-nanquim';
